PipeCraft is an independent runtime dependency. Its source is not vendored in
the Styler repository; architecture-specific Styler release bundles may include a
compiled private PipeCraft binary together with this license notice. PipeCraft owns DAG scheduling, global resource
coordination, process supervision, cancellation, events and durable job/resume
state. Styler owns Linux/domain semantics, receipts, backups, reconciliation,
Apply/Undo meaning and the user interface.

The historical local Python runtime remains temporarily only as an explicit test
and compatibility harness while remaining in-process model dependencies are
removed. Production mutation flows fail closed when PipeCraft is unavailable.
